  "summary": "The Indus (Harappan) civilisation reached its peak between 2600 and 1900 BCE, with sites across modern Pakistan and north-west India; about 1500 settlements are known. Its planned cities, such as Mohenjo-daro and Harappa, were linked by trade. Its script remains unread, so its own voice is lost.",
